opper for sampling colors from the screen.\",{\"children\":\"A whiteboard or drawing app needs presets and an eye dropper for sampling colors from the screen.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Accessibility\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"The color area is a 2D slider with a value text such as \\\"Saturation 60%, brightness 80%\\\", and the hue and opacity tracks are sliders too. Arrow keys move the thumbs, Shift moves in larger steps, Page Up and Page Down jump, and Home and End go to the bounds. The hex input commits on Enter and reverts on Escape, presets are toggle buttons named after their color, and the eye dropper only renders where the browser supports it. The popover is a dialog that receives focus when it opens, closes on Escape or an outside click, and returns focus to the trigger. With reduced motion enabled, the thumb glide, loupe, shake and chip morph are turned off.\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}],[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"How do I add a color picker to a React app?\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"How do I add a color picker to a React app?\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-1\",\"children\":\"Install ColorPicker and compose the parts you need, such as ColorPickerArea, ColorPickerHue, ColorPickerAlpha and ColorPickerHexInput. For a popover, put them in ColorPickerContent next to a ColorPickerTrigger.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Can I control the color value?\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Can I control the color value?\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-1\",\"children\":\"Yes. Pass value and onValueChange for controlled use, or defaultValue for uncontrolled use. onValueChange fires during dragging and